From 55fda4df54ceae3a24d1722b6c28a7cf649a7463 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:35:54 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tools): a short-flute meridian steps out to the full
 radius

Tool::meridian() ended a sharp taper or a drill at the cone top when the
flute was shorter than the cone. Tool::profile() steps out to the full
radius there. The ball nose and the bull nose had the same gap when the
flute was shorter than the corner. The meridian now adds the radial
shoulder (fl, r), as #3929 did for the flat and ball taper tips. The
shoulder is a flat segment, so Meridian::atoms adds no atom and the
solid law pairing does not change. A tool whose flute reaches the full
radius keeps the same meridian points.

Fixes #3938

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
